      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Subgraph federated learning (subgraph-FL) is a new distributed paradigm that facilitates the collaborative training of graph neural networks (GNNs) by multi-client subgraphs.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:bf9ef69924cb50e9d74b731ac4ea9603d31f42da4283237ea8e7b3ac1667c1e5",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "a05a44026cf1f9edf05feb8f9184fddd610f5615b73656d975eadc69f0633d61",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:52.436825Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:a253acbecd09062a8da91c61259923f1c66505bfc08415dc730d6b09f5b74bb0#results[2];abstract[0:174]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4401024865",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "This paper breaks the limits of existing knowledge by proposing Universal Graph Convolution (UniGC), a novel graph convolution concept that re-conceptualizes different graph convolutions as its special cases.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:cb4972495aeaf2aa250b342b67b8af4e1ff6e5a8a7152f14ecb14494993407d9",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "a8fd9ac1c3d78d93c9d758d9a89e87f68f15f6136e380620eb4c12c722c28515",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:31.270655Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:fb56ee1d7b4705234c76cc11b575a973c2afa4a00d0200c55f36f7bbaf4161ff#results[19];abstract[273:481]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393148536",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "We consider graph representation learning in an unsupervised manner.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:cc13273c24ba1b315134ae1090d6696f7d5ec9738aa13d5fcdebc3c32289da10",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "4bc1494aecd03e3bc99a8aedff861a84bed347afdc00983b8cc46b1e4f5cf179",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:09.168460Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:43787e74995b3cb837ea01a73e40b900d0ad0d8c218fe73989f5709a66f3f134#results[36];abstract[0:68]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4285601971",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Recent studies have shown that Graph Convolutional Networks (GCNs) are vulnerable to adversarial attacks on the graph structure.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:d1dcaad7a8251ef76bacdce99ace5876df4a7b24dae3ad06153321acaac0599e",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "ff06d1ac9758308e9d9c446438ffd59512e85b019a621d31a203f2e31bb9c2a3",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:50.458970Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:3a74def3d95207a16576f6b35f0986661472be07a601fe83ecee17a003968dc0#results[3];abstract[0:128]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3189215930",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Motivated the equivalence between the graph learning objective on an attribute graph and the spectral clustering objective on the attribute-interpolated graph, the node attributes are first abstracted as another type of node to harmonize the node attributes and graph topology.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:daf414f0e3f8dacf64957b911c115421c0e6d384fc24fa3155c444bcb5b70215",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "c3200b2f58f42e4a1dea5dfdf9b361608992c011ec7ad2b155981b07f71b5f6b",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:44.933965Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:01c5059546762c3da721da5af276fce8cf7d8c5a7378467ccbce1634623ca92d#results[38];abstract[662:939]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409363851",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To address the issues, we propose a novel personalized framework, DFedHP, in which each client utilizes a hypernetwork to generate the shared part of model parameters and train the personalized parameters separately.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:e9a2f2c1306cf2542c3bd651eeadffd78888d4ae4c4ab9d3d9e69a69cec84c6e",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "98a43269b5615bc10ee8e17b2e5a83e867eab2234fe4e0ae2f2f59e00b4ab4c9",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:30:58.635160Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:880ea8991a7ed694ec99249c8fdb4f958f2aeb27342678b512ce45f7cdbba58c#results[7];abstract[553:769]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4414359927",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Besides, we develop a Graph-Evolving Meta-Learning (GEML) framework that learns to evolve the commonsense graph for reasoning disease-symptom correlations in a new disease, which effectively alleviates the needs of a large number of dialogues.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:f12713ea9100effe692180e9be3dc18f90db8f8afb5ca70e91edf1d555e73e07",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "281469776a6ef84c17bc67fb86c1c020db24910aa570baed16c9752f6baee30c",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:25:21.698827Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:45b817f6b306d66546d473a504d56912ef9fd892acd4daa960825a0c3896c566#results[18];abstract[725:968]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3114290355",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "This paper introduces efficient message passing mechanisms to the graph neural networks with structural prior knowledge to address these problems.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:f139f0db42f11da653805d625f6f63335927eecd6c209264f23383910ee15fd4",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "a8ca3b780595892bb1af3dd0f61eb83759f9e254583f19fbbb157f6c1c32ae41",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:24:49.448016Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:56995f1ad67748f6afb28464e49d0020fd1e00961cb40ef786f12d90e4f8c79d#results[21];abstract[659:805]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3121353543",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "By interpreting Graph Neural Networks (GNNs) as the message passing from the spatial perspective, their success is attributed to Laplacian smoothing.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:f667bf4537af7a623c1f0cf6509919a1122f4d90b421365e2340725635eb7c56",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "a2b3a3731bc711d062cd6bade3e0026cf6018a960d0a7ba6f18bf6594854666b",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:25:47.884955Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:27722257ade4a65d7e519aedfb72edd323591db03ece6e9136e6abd7a76a4c65#results[34];abstract[0:149]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4283805230",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Existing methods based on graph neural networks learn a deterministic embedding function, which lacks sufficient flexibility to explore better choices when dealing with the imperfect and noisy KGs such as the scarce labeled nodes and noisy graph structure.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:fa81e84f41c515638c7549a1610aed330a984a1398b7c9cf4ac0b3add8e979b6",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
