      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4283804765",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "GRASP defines similarities with different meanings between patients for different clinical tasks, and finds similar patients with useful information accordingly, and then learns cohort representation to extract valuable knowledge contained in the similar patients.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:69560001f223f59442ebe2deed2bea7c77ea21d0bea908822103b5366bda9778",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "8aabca571681d8c08626efe8862b44633c355350b37212bdb59f7ca7c635ef5e",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:24:20.913838Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:d38b96d4b5116eac6fe4db56eb934bd79fb6eed83f95fecf80029ee7497fd651#results[12];abstract[767:1031]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3177373898",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Many meta-learning models for few-shot classification elaborately design various task-shared inductive bias (meta-knowledge) to solve such tasks, and achieve impressive performance.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:6ed54c40cc64e71b58184f41cbf005e6833b3e3496198f532b7f83d5c104fa92",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "901f7f2dd65e75c7aa5faa3ef6a77a0d9849aa66b93f7c5224a7b2a54e79a9c0",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:46.255898Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:e8046418608797ced9d25e50fe776721ee5484ddb1b82219258b7e564b5f5094#results[5];abstract[99:280]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3189329097",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "In particular, visual prototypes are obtained by aggregating the local feature maps of the support images, using an attention mechanism that relies on the label embeddings.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:712c3ee21cd56f10b9fa2fdedcf1ffc399e6188d690e4162b121007cc901d3fb",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "e437a65356197b605087e235abf99320a01b7221c6cba689e0e1c9016fb3f237",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:25:41.082498Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:1006cc8a44818b4cefc731788cd38802f557ae377d547125cc57d3af8bb065b9#results[33];abstract[642:814]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3215828051",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "To relieve this problem, recent works adopt self-training teacher-student frameworks to gradually refine the training labels and improve the generalization ability of NER models.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:7167d3787e52ebce09f1b3a2e81c02cbdc5ce3781ac86025148dce9120c62433",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "10c9e6e8c9e69506cfcde22dc45f442641d1b0e184bc5f78f53cacb3ff75b389",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:10.993792Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:a4cc449473053a79e50ca3a7e36f69f6aac5b2ad38b157facaa47abd66a920e2#results[14];abstract[318:496]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382317671",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "We then train our network with the Intra-Video Contrastive loss to make our positive and negative samples more discriminative.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:737e64dafe75f34f2c9158dbbf753d943e76fe4600c9488a4d97f767da01ba2d",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "7fef8c530923a374c6cfc17a7f4d5ab595934a1bbe1ac34ce0f454c3db802538",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:25:43.482458Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:b4d4bfac5bd13cae5bc8e4c634fffabb7131b1fdbb07d54b389f3174315f544c#results[2];abstract[1014:1140]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4283814553",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "The challenge of self-supervised learning lies in fitting high-quality signal representations solely from input signals.",
