      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382240632",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "The compressed features generated by the image encoder are injected convolutional inductive bias and are fed to the Transformer for image classification bypassing image reconstruction.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:d6809715b86d2483e8462b2b9836ece10754e55d78aed656ac39441ce1423edc",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "b55215b8948022bc06b3aa5e03c1eca72a6c2d9a429efb35b76136456e2cc1f7",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:25:27.770480Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:2ba51594f3adae0fc9ae4875b449f6b5632b2f38b254c1db49ee4ef8369b73ac#results[9];abstract[633:817]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4225619305",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "That is, there exists a subset of input image patches such that a ViT can be trained from scratch by using only this subset of patches and achieve similar accuracy to the ViTs trained by using all image patches.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:daab254afcc6a69a589d6d20b666114c4975291cd9ebfbd5420c422fc30bef2a",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "d70da3a715b527643a78154b1317369548340dfb93e7eb20ae919228c48495e8",
