      "source_locator": "openalex-request:1ad9f0ddb54c712a6fedda2ddb92d76f852412ee648e8e975c55886287a13d2e#results[47];abstract[80:326]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409368350",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Moreover, we introduce a spatial compatibility attention bias into the self-attention/cross-attention mechanism for KVPFormer to better model the spatial interactions between entities.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:dd0aa6b0043d29971899b79434a2a8347e631f2165ba81afb6aa66e96b2bb0b5",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "2f0fca5dc29f7174650aa5d96388b2d4307b0a6f130733414e10debfdff1a302",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:27:09.350772Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:80e359606b05e96e8fad17731619ae1d28ac32962b7ddcad600df6755fe6fe29#results[23];abstract[904:1088]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382202584",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Most of the unsupervised hashing methods learn to map images into semantic similarity-preserving hash codes by constructing local semantic similarity structure from the pre-trained model as the guiding information, i.e., treating each point pair similar if their distance is small in feature space.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:de0dbfb6cee82cf1bf599a7a9e6228a6eb65a8917e9553426404b54b21dab4ae",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "c3200b2f58f42e4a1dea5dfdf9b361608992c011ec7ad2b155981b07f71b5f6b",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:44.933965Z",
