      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3187985423",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "In addition, we construct the first publicly available dataset specifically designed for text-to-hand image generation.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:df01265cadfcb8dc994073787320fc03aeff952122fbb3bae3958cbd9cdf4bec",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "5a775517a3756a0af99d326c6e37779c4f0c0d6b0f20a22e3308462661f5a519",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:54.335866Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:eded01a84a6a5b149512ecdd0bfb4c31f26d9b1ece9cd07895f2acc69789e9dd#results[20];abstract[1302:1421]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409365378",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Most contrastive learning methods utilize carefully designed augmentations to generate different movement patterns of skeletons for the same semantics.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:e319f185811b98b885e6c82c0fa5584036c54a445b415e0c3b83e28c9a774dba",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "6909c7889866945433f83df6872cf745c975d068309e4e526d6b6b3395670705",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:26:38.516028Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:e10fbbceba1b077a14fb4bd78ac6fe8e9fa5466450f893e2884c7e0cd3c7163f#results[3];abstract[103:254]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382240124",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "We hypothesize that better contextual representations can be generated from the Transformer with richer positional information.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:e565aec200ff3c3c35fc6d9dd2edd46102666c1238702b8015f29a84b6bf6686",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "42a914d02381733eee64c05206ff29683efcb34537e43afd49281d1a686c0761",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:25:18.028499Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:5160fe6c0ee6997af9d8879f30b410b928594e0f296e250fdd46138368bf8fac#results[36];abstract[248:375]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W3112776819",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "For each learning iteration within one training step, R-STKT aims to filter and rectify the erroneous knowledge contained in the old model and transfer the rectified knowledge to facilitate the short-term learning of the new model.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:e7c78f0aa5c2f6ee798c44a47c8a610673ca613d83e1007358055c9def999e23",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "7161b272923bcbc7b9fe42eff9194c702f77f458978d335d7720ebdc72537556",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:07.585355Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:6deb08c4968a7971197f8e0e674480daa44bc614741d3599def8f5ffc85ab362#results[11];abstract[963:1194]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4393147319",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "We propose to inpaint the background first and develop a two-stage multi-layered latent diffusion framework to edit each element independently.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:e8e4119d2ddd088f87fcd0038d8fff7c6c53d73230918ea147d35009bbc8ba58",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "fcc8d244fa950248335ce17c26efe455d7834abe2a3f164d7ca74522ffec3e8e",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:28:35.111764Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:1ad9f0ddb54c712a6fedda2ddb92d76f852412ee648e8e975c55886287a13d2e#results[23];abstract[454:597]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409368397",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Universal domain adaptation (UniDA) transfers knowledge from a labelled source domain to an unlabelled target domain under domain-shift and category-shift for annotation.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:e9653a8fcba899e79f3416fffbba051787fcce1eeed26ef2094031e814a0a07c",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "e5e50196fcdc4c3ea7ae85154a41cf79f3e19ab73d603ec5da8a68abcdc8540f",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:29:13.693777Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:fb666590c409a515a530c348e30cfd9a685e5720d6d0225efd0ad0df53def1ad#results[32];abstract[0:170]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4409364519",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "Then, we devise three layers to progressively obtain patient-level representation, including a local-level interaction layer adopting Manhattan distance, a WSI-level interaction layer employing spatial shuffle, and a patient-level interaction layer using attention pooling.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:f63c759031bf2b90cfb31bf626c0a3f6976aac3cdc9c80d28f102dac50bf1b78",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
      "raw_sha256": "1a9936289698a6d1b81ed81c75f8084d90da5ea7416accb4e37a552905a8bce1",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-11-07T20:26:33.592906Z",
      "source_locator": "openalex-request:a5fc104bf42bed3fa16a6ccd67147fb492715ccd07dd48bd78f33c182653375b#results[10];abstract[898:1171]",
      "source_url": "https://openalex.org/W4382460188",
      "support_edge_ids": [],
      "support_paper_ids": []
    },
    {
      "excerpt": "(3) Thirdly, Based on the STS-B and SICK benchmarks, we find that two sentences with consistent semantics tend to share similar parameter activation patterns in deep layers, which aligns with our third finding.",
      "id": "evidence:topic:f6be5a9b4e7bc9e3044df8d224112da057a8e8bd0e64e2f6e1066b516a91c695",
      "kind": "inferred_topic",
